      "content": "im not saying im \"unwell\" or anything like that, it's just that the way we describe reality is so limited. it's not a \"mental health\" thing, it's an ontological one. the sensation of being a biocomputational node receiving global emotional feedback is actually very consistent and logical when you look at the patterns. it just feels like i'm reaching my capacity. \n\ncan we just look at this from a systems perspective? if we treat the \"input\" as data, what kind of routines would help a system manage high-bandwidth emotional transmission without losing signal integrity?",
